    "top_section": "REMOTE WORK POLICY",
    "retrieval_seconds": 0.4699661909980932,
    "answer_seconds": 9.21565820199612,
    "total_seconds": 9.685670831007883,
    "answer": "Based on ACME policies, the following protections and requirements apply to a privileged administrator working remotely:\n\n**Access and System Security** (*INFORMATION SECURITY POLICY*):\n* **Privileged Access Control:** Privileged access (admin/root) requires Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA). Access follows least privilege, requires individual and auditable accounts (no shared/generic accounts), and is reviewed and recertified quarterly.\n* **Endpoint & Data Encryption:** Laptops must have full-disk encryption enabled (BitLocker for Windows or FileVault for Mac). All data in transit must use TLS 1.2 or higher, and data at rest must be encrypted using AES-256.\n* **Password Standards:** Passwords must be at least 12 characters (including uppercase, lowercase, numbers, and special characters), expire every 90 days, and cannot reuse the last 12 passwords.\n\n**Usage and Remote Work Controls**:\n* **Security Controls & Devices** (*ACCEPTABLE USE POLICY*): Circumventing security controls (such as VPN bypass or disabling endpoint protection) and storing sensitive data on personal devices are strictly prohibited.\n* **Remote Work Conditions** (*REMOTE WORK POLICY*): Remote work requires manager agreement (up to 3 days per week after a 6-month probationary period; VP approval for fully remote), maintaining core hours (10:00 AM \u2013 3:00 PM local time), remaining reachable on Slack within 30 minutes during core hours, and obtaining HR/Legal approval before working outside the country of employment.",
